33. 根据 Mundulla Yellows, lime 定位，听到“It wasn’t until 2004 that they found the cause of the problem was lime, ... to give it its proper chemical name, which was being used in the construction of roads;

34. 根据题目前标题定位，听到“ a disease known as “Bell-miner Associated Die-back”. The bell-miner is a bird... it’s the leaves of the trees that are affected. What happens is that insects settle on the leaves and eat their way round them, destroying them as they go...”; settle on 与题干 feed on 同义替换；

35. 根据人名及 high-frequency bushfires 定位, 听到“If there are very frequent bushfires in the region, this encourages grass to grow afterwards. 同义替换：very frequent—high frequency，encourage—result in 对应题干；

36. 根据 mid-frequency bushfires 定位，听到 “Why do fairly frequent bushfifires actually support the growth of eucalyptus. Well, one reason is that the fire stops the growth of other species which would consume water needed by eucalyptus trees”为题干 available to.....的转述，结合预判词性可知为 water;

